{
  "On a tablet and a phone the scheduler keeps its appointments, views and date and shows them another way: a phone gets the agenda, a compact bar and sheets from the bottom; a finger lifts, resizes, swipes and pinches.": "",
  "Three ways to show one scheduler": "",
  "As it is: the bar with Today, the steps, the date and a button per view; the tooltip next to the appointment, the form in a window.": "",
  "As on a desktop, its view kept (a week, as tablet calendars open); on a touch screen everything a finger taps is larger.": "",
  "The agenda (a day when the views have no agenda). The bar holds Today as an icon, the month (opening the calendar) and one menu of the views; a swipe moves between days. The tooltip is an action sheet, the form a sheet from the bottom. A narrower ruler, resource column and time column, so a week still fits the screen; every view works.": "",
  "With `presentation: 'auto'` (the default) it watches its own width and the screen's pointer, as the [TabDocumentManager](/tabdocs/mobile) does: under `phoneWidth` (560) as on a phone, under `tabletWidth` (1024) as on a tablet on a touch screen. Phones are 360 to 430 pixels wide.": "",
  "A finger": "",
  "The listeners are on the scheduler before a finger lands, so a lifted appointment, a swipe and a pinch keep the page still; anything else scrolls natively. After a drag no click follows, and nothing a finger touched stays looking hovered. Open this page on a phone, or with the browser's touch emulation.": "",
  "Its tooltip (an action sheet on a phone): Edit, Delete.": "",
  "Lifts it after a moment and moves it; the page does not scroll while it is lifted. Let go where it may go.": "",
  "It stays selected with a handle in the middle of its start and its end; drag a handle to resize it. A tap elsewhere puts it down.": "",
  "The next or the previous days. A view that can still scroll that way (a wide week, a timeline) scrolls first; at its end the swipe moves on.": "",
  "Zooms the hours of the day views and the cells of a timeline (`timeZoom`, 0.5 to 4).": "",
  "Selects it, then opens the form for a new appointment there.": "",
  "Native scrolling, as everywhere on the page.": "",
  "Everything a gesture does has a button or a key: the month opens the calendar, the arrows move the focused appointment (Shift: its end), N and P the days.": "",
  "The tooltip and the form are dialogs: focus moves in and back, Escape and the back button close them.": "",
  "On a touch screen the bar, the agenda rows and the lines of the month take the language’s large control height.": "",
  "Unit: the bar as on a phone.": "",
  "Unit states: the appointment a finger holds, and the one it let go (with its handles).": "",
  "Unit: a handle, in the middle of an edge; down the side of a bar it is turned.": "",
  "Units: the mark at the side the next days come from while swiping.": "",
  "Plain tokens.": "",
  "Places: the kit’s buttons and sheets inside.": "",
  "How it shows itself: by its own width, or always one way. The appointments, the views and the date stay the same.": "",
  "Under this width (of the scheduler, not of the screen) `auto` shows it as on a phone, whatever the pointer.": "",
  "`'touch'`: as on a tablet only when the screen's pointer is a finger (`(pointer: coarse)`, followed live); `'width'`: the width alone.": "",
  "The view (by name or type) it shows as on a phone; a day when the views have none of it. Going back, it shows the view it had, unless the user chose another. `null` keeps the view.": "",
  "The same, as on a tablet; `null` keeps the view.": "",
  "A finger swiping sideways goes to the next or the previous days.": "",
  "Two fingers zoom the time scale.": "",
  "How far the time scale is zoomed: 1 as the design language sizes it, 0.5 to 4.": "",
  "`{ from, to, width, cancel }`: refused, it keeps showing as it does until the width or the setting changes again.": "",
  "`{ from, to, cancel }`, as two fingers start to zoom; refused, the page zooms instead.": "",
  "`{ from, to }`, when the fingers let go.": "",
  "`e.form` is the window, or on a phone the `BottomSheet` the form comes up in.": "",
  "How it shows itself now: `'desktop'`, `'tablet'` or `'phone'`.": "",
  "The sheets are the kit's [BottomSheet](/bottomsheet) and [ActionSheet](/actionsheet).": ""
}
